      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Spring storms in Utah bring heavy rain, high winds, hail, and rapid snowmelt that frequently cause missing or lifted shingles, dented metal flashing, and\n\ncompromised roof seals. Left unchecked, these vulnerabilities lead to active water leaks and costly structural deterioration inside the home.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "compromised roof seals"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Watch this short news clip showing local storm and wind impacts in Utah:",
        "video": {
          "link": "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/n5Ikcl01Iw8",
          "thumbnail": "https://serpapi.com/images/i/R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAP_______yH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw.gif"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Types of Spring Roof Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "High Wind Uplift: Strong gusts tear away, curl, or crack loose shingles, exposing the underlayment."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hail Impact:\nHailstones bruise or fracture shingle mats and cause prominent granule loss into gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flashing Failures: Severe weather warps metal around chimneys, skylights, and valleys, allowing water to slip through."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Debris Punctures:\nUprooted branches or blown debris scrape and puncture the roof surface."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Steps After a Storm"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect from the Ground: Walk your property's perimeter to check for fallen shingle tabs, dented downspouts, or bruised siding before climbing any ladders.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              8,
              9,
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document Everything: Take clear photographs of any visible exterior damage and compromised gutters for your records.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Beware of Door-Knockers: Avoid signing immediate contracts with out-of-town storm chasers who arrive right after severe weather."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a Professional Evaluation: Reach out to a trusted local contractor (such as through Frame Restoration Utah\nor ) for a certified roof inspection and detailed documentation before filing an insurance claim."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you would like more help, please tell me:"
